# Call-site ledger of aiocache at e673d62e98bf89b619e48f44cd68c96a30d95a1b.
# Hand-written from the source; judgements in aiocache.md.
#
# Sets used below (see aiocache.md, "Value sites"):
#   caches (7): BaseCache (a plain public class, its own receiver),
#     SimpleMemoryBackend, SimpleMemoryCache, MemcachedBackend, MemcachedCache,
#     RedisBackend, RedisCache. The backend methods _add, _get, ... exist in
#     BaseCache (they raise NotImplementedError) and in the three *Backend
#     classes; the *Cache classes inherit them.
#   serializers (6): BaseSerializer (a plain public class), NullSerializer,
#     StringSerializer, PickleSerializer, JsonSerializer, MsgPackSerializer.
#   The alias-config role at factory.py:24 is narrower than the backend
#   serializer-instance role: it has no MsgPackSerializer class witness.
#   plugins (3): BasePlugin, TimingPlugin, HitMissRatioPlugin.
#   command wrappers: base.py:141-456 decorate the 11 commands (add, get,
#     multi_get, set, multi_set, delete, exists, increment, expire, clear,
#     raw) with API.plugins, then API.timeout, then
#     API.aiocache_enabled(...), then API.register. The class attribute of
#     each command is the closure API.aiocache_enabled.enabled._enabled;
#     cache.get(...) calls it, it calls API.timeout._timeout, which calls
#     API.plugins._plugins, which calls the method (BaseCache.get). close is
#     decorated with API.timeout only (base.py:484).
default reject aiocache.base._Conn.__getattr__: _Conn.__getattr__ runs only for an attribute that normal lookup does not find on a _Conn object; no package site loads such an attribute from a _Conn: the receivers are caches, serializers, plugins, locks, decorators, clients of redis or aiomcache, modules, builtins and client objects, and the _Conn methods load only _cache and _conn, which _Conn.__init__ sets

